ROLE: You make literal edits to two TypeScript files. Re-read each first. Make exactly these edits and nothing else.

CONTEXT: In `.skilled/skills/sk-vision/vision-runtime/src/runtime/client.ts`, `close()` does not stop a provisioning subprocess (`uv venv`, `uv pip install`, or the pip fallback) that `runProvision()` started. If that subprocess hangs, it outlives the client and `ready` never settles. Killing it is recoverable: the next start finds `moondream` missing and provisions again, and `uv venv` replaces an existing venv.

ACTION:

1. In `client.ts`, replace these lines:

  // Set by close(); a startup still provisioning when it is set must not spawn.
  private closed = false;

with:

  // Set by close(); a startup still provisioning when it is set must not spawn.
  private closed = false;
  // The provisioning subprocess in flight, so close() can stop it.
  private provisioning: ChildProcess | null = null;

2. In `client.ts`, inside `private async runProvision(`, replace these lines:

    log(`${label}...`);
    await new Promise<void>((resolve, reject) => {
      const child = spawn(cmd, args, { stdio: ["ignore", "pipe", "pipe"] });
      child.stdout.on("data", (d) => log(`  ${d}`));
      child.stderr.on("data", (d) => log(`  ${d}`));
      child.on("error", reject);
      child.on("exit", (code) =>
        code === 0 ? resolve() : reject(new Error(`${label} failed (exit ${code})`)),
      );
    });

with:

    if (this.closed) throw new SkVisionError("SHUTDOWN", "sk-vision runtime closed");
    log(`${label}...`);
    await new Promise<void>((resolve, reject) => {
      const child = spawn(cmd, args, { stdio: ["ignore", "pipe", "pipe"] });
      this.provisioning = child;
      child.stdout.on("data", (d) => log(`  ${d}`));
      child.stderr.on("data", (d) => log(`  ${d}`));
      child.on("error", (err) => {
        this.provisioning = null;
        reject(err);
      });
      child.on("exit", (code) => {
        this.provisioning = null;
        if (code === 0) resolve();
        else reject(new Error(`${label} failed (exit ${code})`));
      });
    });

